# ==============================================================================
# Mosquitto Password File — Example
# ==============================================================================
# Device logins beyond the one in .env (MQTT_USER / MQTT_PASSWORD). Don't edit
# by hand: passwords are hashed. Add or change a login with
#
#   make mqtt-user NAME=<name>          # prompts for the password
#   make mqtt-user-delete NAME=<name>
#
# which write config/mosquitto/passwd (kept out of git), then restart the
# broker: docker compose restart mqtt
#
# The file is used only while MQTT_PASSWORD is set in .env: that is the switch
# that makes the device listeners ask for a login.
#
# Format: username:hashed_password (one per line)
# ==============================================================================

# sensor-001:$7$101$...
# monitor:$7$101$...
